      "expectedViews": [
        "ui://mcp-calculix/results-viewer"
      ],
      "network": {
        "exposure": "loopback-only",
        "composeNetwork": "chain",
        "sharedVolumes": [
          "exports:/exports:ro",
          "casys-digital-thread-calculix-inputs:/inputs",
          "casys-digital-thread-calculix-runs:/var/lib/mcp-calculix-runs"
        ],
        "upstreams": []
      },
      "trust": {
        "level": "first-party-local",
        "executesArbitraryCode": false,
        "notes": [
          "The solver mounts /exports read-only. Generic content-addressed FEA inputs are staged by the Digital Thread into provider-private /inputs on a dedicated volume; it is neither a shared exchange nor evidence. Every solve snapshots its input privately, while only recorded static runs retain evidence in the separate run ledger.",
          "Native meshing and solver processes still require untrusted-input hardening."
        ]
      }
    },
